// Starts one Architect build with the exact requirement of the failed $1.96 build (b8a9e936) so the
// per-call records the server now keeps can be compared like for like. Poll it with measure-build-poll.
String body = '{"requirement": "Build an AI agent for WhatsApp inbound lead capture and qualification with the following flow:\\n\\n1. On incoming WhatsApp message from an unknown customer:\\n   - Check if customer exists (by WhatsApp number or email). If not, create a new Lead with Status = New.\\n   - Send welcome message: \'Hi! Welcome. To help us understand your requirements better, could you please share your name?\'\\n   - Wait for customer reply (name).\\n\\n2. When name is received:\\n   - Update Lead Name.\\n   - Ask for email: \'Thanks, [Name]. Could you please share your email address?\'\\n   - Validate email format. If invalid, ask again.\\n   - Update Lead Email field.\\n\\n3. When email is received and valid:\\n   - Ask for Project Type (show picklist options from Project Type field).\\n   - Wait for customer selection.\\n   - Store selection in Project Type field.\\n\\n4. When Project Type is selected:\\n   - Ask for Project Name (dependent picklist, options based on selected Project Type).\\n   - Validate response against available Project Names for that type.\\n   - If valid, update Project Name field and proceed. If invalid, show available options and ask again. Allow customer to indicate not interested (set Lead Status = Lost Lead).\\n   - As soon as valid Project Name is provided, set Lead Status = WhatsApp Qualified.\\n\\n5. When Project Name is valid:\\n   - Ask for Budget (show picklist options: \'Rs 50L - Rs 1Cr\', \'Rs 1Cr - Rs 2Cr\', \'Rs 2Cr - Rs 5Cr\', \'Rs 5Cr+\').\\n   - Store selection in Budget field.\\n\\n6. After all above:\\n   - Ask to schedule a meeting. Collect date, time, and time zone.\\n   - Create an Event for the meeting.\\n   - Create a Task summarizing all details collected.\\n\\nLead Status transitions:\\n- New: on creation\\n- In Process: when customer responds\\n- Lost Lead: if customer not interested\\n- WhatsApp Qualified: as soon as valid Project Name is provided\\n\\nAll field dependencies (Project Name by Project Type) and picklist values must be dynamically fetched from Salesforce.\\n\\nThe agent should handle all WhatsApp conversations, validations, and Salesforce updates as described.", "maxCostUsd": 4}';
HttpResponse r = ArchonServerClient.callout('POST', '/api/architect/build', body, 60000);
System.debug('MB_START ' + r.getStatusCode() + ' ' + r.getBody().left(200));
